<article class="env-theorem" id="0252">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0252">Theorem <span data-tag="0252">41.9.2</span>.</a> Let $A$, $B$ be Noetherian local rings. Let $f : A \to B$ be a local homomorphism. If $M$ is a finite $B$-module that is flat as an $A$-module, and $t \in \mathfrak m_ B$ is an element such that multiplication by $t$ is injective on $M/\mathfrak m_ AM$, then $M/tM$ is also $A$-flat. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
